This report presents the initial observation of the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_L$ decay mode and provides evidence for the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^0_L$ process. The analysis is based on $3.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ of integrated luminosity from $pp$ collisions at $\gamma\gamma$ center-of-mass energies of 7 and 8 TeV, collected by the LHCb experiment. The measured branching fractions are given as
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{0} K^{\text{L}} &)=
(4.41\pm 0.53\pm 0.15)\times 10\\%,\end{align\}
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{B}(B^0_s\to\bar{D}^{*0} K^{\text{L}} &)=
(5.7\pm 0.7\pm 0.2)\times 10\\%,
\end{align*}
where the first uncertainties are statistical and the second systematic. These results incorporate recently updated decay widths for the $b\to c$ semileptonic modes.
